{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/gender-gap",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "gender gap"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "Gender difference/gap is understood as an observable and measurable disparity between women and men or girls and boys in terms of participation, access to resources, rights, benefits, opportunities, or social outcomes."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "A difference does not necessarily constitute inequality, but it may indicate its presence when it is systematic and linked to gender-related norms, roles, and social structures. In the case of persons with disabilities, gender differences should be analysed intersectionally, as gender and disability may jointly shape distinct experiences and social positions. Gender differences can be examined through sex- or gender-based comparisons in areas such as education, employment, income, health, autonomy, safety, care, access to services, and participation in decision-making, while taking the type of disability into account."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "7.4.1"
  ],
